00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:25.360
was to really celebrate what
developers and operators

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.155
actually do every day.

00:01:27.155 --> 00:01:28.780
Hopefully, they're
spending hours a day

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.690
productively, building apps,
running apps, deploying apps,

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:35.355
monitoring apps, and not
dealing with all the other stuff

00:01:35.355 --> 00:01:37.730
that you normally have to do
when you build applications,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.780
especially in the enterprise.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.110
Getting out of waterfall
and getting to agile,

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:45.288
not just throwing over--

00:01:45.288 --> 00:01:47.330
an app over the wall for
someone else to operate,

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:50.950
but taking ownership in a
DevOps culture and operating.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.990
And really removing
all the barriers,

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:57.340
everything from not having to
manage and shard databases, not

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:02.110
have to manually manage your
VMs, or even pick VM sizes,

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:05.187
and really just get to the
heart of building applications,

00:02:05.187 --> 00:02:07.270
and then let the cloud
take care of it from there.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.662
That was the spirit we wanted
to capture in the keynote.

00:02:10.662 --> 00:02:13.120
STEPHANIE WONG: So configuring
networks, rewriting apps due

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.470
